# Build context for the ingestion image.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the shared `.dockerignore`,
# which is why this file exists: the shared one excludes `pipelines/` to keep it
# out of the Go API image, and that is exactly what this image is built from.
#
# Without this file the ingest build would receive no source at all — and it
# would fail at COPY rather than produce a broken image, but only after pulling
# and installing everything first.
.git
.idea
.env

# Never let a local virtualenv or cache into the image: uv installs from the
# lockfile, and copied-in bytecode from another platform would shadow it.
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache

# Not needed at runtime. The tests run in CI against the source tree, not in
# this image.
pipelines/tests
docs
*.md

# Go sources, the compiled dataset archives and the raw downloads. The raw
# directory in particular holds hundreds of megabytes of PDFs and XML that a
# pipeline re-fetches when it needs them.
cmd
internal
api
dist
pipelines/data

# db/ is deliberately absent from the list above, even though nothing in this
# image executes SQL. `dataset export` stamps the newest migration filename into
# MANIFEST.json, and `dataset import` refuses an archive whose stamp does not
# match the schema in front of it.
#
# Excluding it made latest_migration() fall back to "unknown", so an archive cut
# inside the container was rejected on import anywhere else — a schema mismatch
# reported against a perfectly good archive, on the self-hosting path this
# release exists for. 28 KB of SQL is a cheap fix.
